🔹 Conceptual Questions
11.	What data structure is used for cycle detection?
Disjoint Set Union (DSU), also known as Union-Find.
12.	Why is Kruskal’s algorithm greedy?
Because it always picks the smallest weight edge that doesn’t form a cycle.
13.	Can Kruskal’s algorithm work with negative edge weights?
Yes, it only compares edge weights and doesn't require them to be positive.
14.	Why is the total number of selected edges always V-1?
Because a spanning tree of a graph with V vertices has exactly V - 1 edges.

