Algorithm Steps:
Sort all edges of the graph in increasing order of weight.

Initialize:

Create a disjoint set (Union-Find) for all vertices (each vertex is in its own set initially).

Set MST edge count = 0 and total cost = 0.

For each edge (u, v) in sorted edge list:

If find(u) ≠ find(v) (i.e., u and v are in different sets):

Add edge (u, v) to the MST.

Perform union(u, v) to merge the sets.

Increment edge count and update total cost.

Stop when MST contains (V - 1) edges.
